      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{8}=71$ and ${a}_{20}=191.$ What is the common difference of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *increasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *positive*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{8}=71,\\,{a}_{20}=191.\n$$\n\nTo find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=20$ and $m=8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{20}-{a}_{8}}{20-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{191-71}{20-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{12} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=10.$",
